//static.wikia.nocookie.net/memoryalpha/images/3/39/Site-community-image/revision/latest?cb=20241212154521&path-prefix=en","description":"A dancer was a person who danced either professionally as a form of entertainment, or non-professionally for recreational or formal purposes. One who danced with another was known as a dance partner. The Orion Marta was a self-described “wonderful dancer;” Garth of Izar concurred, even calling her “a superb dancer”. (TOS: “Whom Gods Destroy”) According to Mister Flint, in 2269, Rayna was “a most accomplished dancer.” (TOS: “Requiem for Methuselah”) Dr. Beverly Crusher was an award-winning…","url":"https://memory-alpha.fandom.com/wiki/Dancer"}}]},"2373573":{"original_name":"Ashley McDonogh","totalityOfRoles":[{"credit_type":"cast","department":"Acting","job":"Actor","media":{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/cm3srKkyVn8zUK40ox8ZNjRJRdE.jpg","id":580,"name":"Star Trek: Deep Space Nine","original_name":"Star Trek: Deep Space Nine","overview":"At Deep Space Nine, a space station located next to a wormhole in the vicinity of the liberated planet of Bajor, Commander Sisko and crew welcome alien visitors, root out evildoers and solve all types of unexpected problems that come their way.","poster_path":"/vE6138ykaEXQkCSEHyuBIgfGlUZ.jpg","media_type":"tv","original_language":"en","genre_ids":[10765,10759,18],"popularity":39.2846,"first_air_date":"1993-01-03","vote_average":7.892,"vote_count":896,"origin_country":["US"],"character":"Dorian Collins","episodes":[{"id":1005849,"name":"Valiant","overview":"Stardate: 51825.4. Jake and Nog's runabout comes under attack from the Jem'Hadar. They are rescued by the Valiant, a ship manned by Red Squad, a elite group of young Starfleet cadets.","media_type":"tv_episode","vote_average":6.8,"vote_count":24,"air_date":"1998-05-06","episode_number":22,"episode_type":"standard","production_code":"40510-546","runtime":45,"season_number":6,"show_id":580,"still_path":"/1HS7nybuygJzUI6anqxJjzFbWdb.jpg"}],"season